---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/archive.css';

// PERMANENT ARCHIVE PAGE. Styling comes from src/styles/archive.css, which is
// theme-INDEPENDENT on purpose. Do not re-theme this page during a rebuild.
//
// Edward asked for this one to be kept forever (2026-08-21). The mp4 in
// public/video/ is a roske.ai copy of interRel's upload, same reasoning as the
// Eddie and the Consultants archive: he no longer controls that channel.
//
// The Kscope17 label in the filename is interRel's, and it is provably wrong.
// The real year is UNCONFIRMED. Do not assert one without asking Edward.

const YOUTUBE = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F-mS4LsjPI0';
const FILE = '/video/this-is-me-kscope17.mp4';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="This Is Me: interRel at Kscope | Roske.AI"
  description="interRel performs This Is Me from The Greatest Showman at ODTUG Kscope, in full costume, in a hotel ballroom. Edward Roske plays the Bearded Lady. Archived copy of the original interRel recording."
  ogImage="/images/this-is-me/poster.jpg"
>
  <link slot="head" rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link slot="head" rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link slot="head" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,500;0,700;0,900;1,500&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

  <div class="arc arc-showman">

    <section class="arc-top">
      <div class="arc-wrap">
        <div class="arc-eyebrow">
          <span class="arc-pip"></span>ARCHIVE . KSCOPE . THE BEARDED LADY
        </div>
        <h1 class="arc-h1">This Is Me</h1>
        <p class="arc-sub">interRel does The Greatest Showman</p>
        <div class="arc-rule"></div>
        <p class="arc-lede">
          4 minutes of a consulting company performing the big number from The Greatest Showman in full
          costume, on the patterned carpet of a hotel ballroom, at an Oracle technology conference, with
          the confetti already down before anyone starts singing. I am the Bearded Lady. I'd rather say
          that at the top than have you work it out on your own around the 90 second mark. (Edward, you
          were running an Oracle consulting firm at the time, with a booth to staff and a pipeline to
          close, and you spent part of that conference in a beard and a costume, and now, years later,
          you have gone and put the footage on your own website. Nobody is making you do this.)
        </p>

        <figure class="arc-player">
          <video
            controls
            preload="metadata"
            playsinline
            poster="/images/this-is-me/poster.jpg"
            src={FILE}
            width="1280"
            height="720"
          ></video>
          <figcaption>
            Shot by somebody in the crowd on a phone. That's the correct way to record this, and I
            wouldn't take a cleaner copy if one turned up.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="arc-actions">
          <a class="arc-btn" href={FILE} download>Download the file (mp4)</a>
          <a class="arc-btn arc-btn-ghost" href={YOUTUBE} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch the original on YouTube</a>
          <a class="arc-btn arc-btn-ghost" href="/video/">The rest of the archive</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="arc-sec arc-sec-alt">
      <div class="arc-wrap arc-wrap-narrow">
        <h2 class="arc-h2">A note on the year</h2>
        <p class="arc-body">
          interRel posted this as Kscope17. Kscope17 ran June 25 to 29 of 2017, and This Is Me wasn't
          released until October 26 of that year, so one of those two things is wrong and it isn't the
          song. My guess is Kscope18. For a show whose entire thesis is that the outcasts were right all
          along, staging it for a ballroom of Essbase administrators was either the perfect audience or a
          cry for help, and I have never been able to decide which.
        </p>
        <p class="arc-body">
          This is the second musical number on this site. Most consulting firms manage zero, and I'm
          aware that clearing that bar twice says more about me than it does about the firms. The other
          one runs 58 minutes and has an Aquaman in it, so by the standards of this archive, 4 minutes of
          me in a beard is the restrained entry.
        </p>
        <p class="arc-body">
          If you were in that ballroom and you remember which year you watched your consulting vendor
          perform a circus number at you, Edward@Roske.AI. I would genuinely like to know!
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Circus red, a shade hotter than the archive default. Both modes declared so
     the toggle and the OS preference each land somewhere legible. */
  .arc-showman { --arc-accent: #a3202b; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :global(html:not([data-theme='light'])) .arc-showman { --arc-accent: #e8757c; }
  }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .arc-showman { --arc-accent: #e8757c; }
</style>
